    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n7526" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cercyo</span></b> , ŏnis,
			m., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κερκυών</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a celebrated robber in
				Attica</i>, <i>conquered and slain by Theseus at
				Eleusis</i>, <i><span class="en">Ov. M. 7, 439</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Hyg. Fab.
				187</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Gell. 15, 21, 1</span></i>.—<i>Acc.</i> Gr. Cercyona, <i><span class="en">Stat. Th.
				12, 577</span></i>.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Cercyŏnē-us</span></b> , a,
				um, adj., <i>pertaining to
				Cercyon</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">corpora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. Ib.
					410</span></i>
			.</div>
